# Client apps (dashboard, web, mobile)

## All clients

- Call the API only. No direct PostgreSQL. No Prisma.
- Keep business logic in the API, not in the client.
- Do not duplicate API business logic in the client.
- Show loading, error, and empty states on data screens.
- Show readable errors when API calls fail.
- Frontend hiding is not authorization — the API must enforce access.

## Dashboard (`apps/dashboard`)

- Internal admin tool. Function over polish.
- Paginate large tables. Do not load MapLibre on pages without a map.
- Reuse existing review and page-shell patterns before new one-off UIs.
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod where the app already does.
- Centralize API calls (e.g. `src/lib/api.ts`).

## Web (`apps/web`)

- Public map: MapLibre GL JS + PMTiles basemap.
- Tiles for rendering. API for search, details, routing, auth, and user data.
- Do not load all regional PMTiles at once.
- Keep MapLibre code separate from business rules.
- Do not break existing Myanmar font and glyph support.
- On mobile web, prefer top search + bottom sheet over wide sidebars.

## Mobile (`apps/mobile`)

- Same rules as web: API only, no database access.
